## Predigit / Carry Verdict
free_hole_doublet_predigits=2 held events, both later emitted as 2 doublet certificates
owner_boundary_predigits=1 bypass event, emitted only with HYP-3520/HYP-3522 sidecars
untyped_pending_carry=0
typed_residual_carry=(45,173)
route_guard=HYP-3513 requires route sidecar R unless route reconstruction is proved
vertical_guard=vertical halfturn remains an address projection, not a sheet gluing

## Proof Pull
P1: Formalize ordinary route certificates as immediate spigot digits.
P2: Formalize HYP-3511 doublet buffering: first half is a predigit, second half emits the doublet certificate.
P3: Formalize bypass emission as owner-filtration carry: transport (23,93,113), bracket lift (147,169), residual (45,173).
P4: Attach HYP-3513 route sidecar R and vertical guard to every emitted certificate before any quotient compression.

## Tournament Analysis
vertices=proof-output states and carry buffers, not runners, arcs, or raw witness counts
pairwise_observable=no-backtracking terminal emission with named carry
switch=higher emission safety and lower unresolved carry
score_hist={10: 1, 100: 1, 61: 1, 77: 1, 82: 1, 86: 1, 91: 1, 93: 1}
directed_3cycles=0
scc_sizes=[1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1]
hamiltonian_path=certificate_spigot_state_machine -> free_hole_doublet_predigit_buffer -> owner_filtration_carry_buffer -> private_firewall_route_guard -> vertical_halfturn_guard -> ordinary_immediate_route_digit -> static_terminal_ledger -> raw_count_shadow

## Assumption Challenge
Considered vertices: runners, raw arcs, witness cells, legal components, terminal certificates, output positions, carry buffers, free-hole packets, owner rows, route sidecars, vertical quotient guards, and proof obligations.
Chosen vertices are output states plus carry buffers.  This preserves the random031 terminal predicate while deliberately forgetting raw runner order only after branch/u order, terminal class, owner carry, bracket carry, route guard, and vertical guard are retained.
